  "description": "VITNAR crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C52 H64 N4 O24 Tb4,2(C2 H3 N1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb1A (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2A (Tb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.583-3.774 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.04-104.48°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C56H74N6O26Tb4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
